    "gh_6f4d0a1c5dabd825edd7a35f": {
      "id": "gh_6f4d0a1c5dabd825edd7a35f",
      "sourceId": "remote-job-boards/software-engineering#7462",
      "title": "REO: Senior iOS Engineer",
      "description": "**Tags:** #ios #swift #ui #ci&cd #functional-programming #design #senior #engineer #digital-nomad #ios\n\n**Published on:** October 27, 2021\n\n**Original Job Post:** https://remoteOK.io/remote-jobs/106857-remote-senior-ios-engineer-reo\n\n![](https://remoteOK.io/assets/img/jobs/106731f8263f217e92b5530e393aa1b21635330341.png)\n\nAt [REO](http://reo.so) we want to help real estate brokers, owners and buyers find and trade properties easier than ever. We believe that easy-to-use software is key in this complex and fast-paced industry.\n\nWe are looking for a Senior iOS Engineer to further accelerate our development. We offer a competitive salary and REO stock options (ESOP) making you a true owner in our vision. \n\n## Your responsibilities\n\nTake ownership during refinement and planning to break down new epics into small deliverables.\n\nParticipate in the design process to jointly deliver the product quickly and with high quality.\n\nShip features every two weeks or quicker.\n\nResponsible for the quality of the iOS app and proposing strategic and lasting improvements. \n\n## Your profile\n\nYou have experience in Swift, programmatic UI, and basic reactive programming.\n\nYou like learning quickly and seeing the impact that your work has.\n\nYou consider the perspective of the user and company, when proposing new ideas. Why we do something is just as important as what we do. \n\nYou have extensive experience in testing and in building up a CI/CD pipeline.\n\nYou are driven by real impact of your work. You don't require a large team to make things happen.\n\n## Technical Stack\n\n100 % Swift\n\nVanilla SwiftUI with UIKit wrappers\n\nCombine\n\nApollo iOS (GraphQL Client)\n\nSPM\n\nSemaphore\n\n## Culture\n\nAt REO we put a lot of emphasis on impact, speed, and user value. We also take time to find better ways to work, use new tools and adopt new technologies — for us, this is an essential part of work. Knowledge shares happen every 4 weeks and everyone can present their topic of choice. \n\nWe are based in [Berlin](https://www.google.com/maps/place/Niebuhrstra%C3%9Fe+78,+10629+Berlin/@52.5039463) but are a distributed team. Learn more about how we work and what we strive for at our [careers page](https://reo.so/careers). \n\nDo you have questions or want to get in touch? Send us a line to [<span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"dcbfbdaeb9b9aeaf9caeb9b3f2afb3\">[email protected]</span>](mailto:<span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"1c7f7d6e79796e6f5c6e7973326f73\">[email protected]</span>)\t\n\nBe sure to mention the words **POPULAR BEACH JOURNEY** when applying to show you read the job post completely. This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words\tto find applicants that read this and see they're human.\n\n\t\n\n#Salary and compensation\nNo salary data published by company so we estimated salary based on previous jobs related to . $60,000 — $100,000/year\n\n\n### Location\n🌏 Worldwide<br>",
